From: Sleepy <sleepy@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: fall back to DRM-core AMD VSDB FreeSync info

The amdgpu-side parse_hdmi_amd_vsdb() relies on the DMUB/DMCU firmware to
report the AMD VSDB (dc_edid_parser_send_cea + DMUB_CMD__EDID_CEA). On some
RDNA4 parts the firmware does not detect the AMD VSDB, so
vsdb_info.freesync_supported stays false and the connector reports
vrr_capable=0 even though the display advertises FreeSync (AMD VSDB v1/v2).

drm_edid.c (patch 0050) already parses the AMD VSDB directly and populates
connector->display_info.amd_vsdb (freesync_supported, min/max frame rate,
freesync_vcp_code) for v1/v2/v3. Use that as a fallback in
amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps() when the firmware path found nothing, and
also populate sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code + mccs_caps.freesync_supported
so the later freesync_vcp_code/mccs reset in the same function does not undo
the fallback result.

Signed-off-by: Sleepy <sleepy@localhost>
Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index 9a80c41095fc..22d95de6b91b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -3928,6 +3928,46 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(struct drm_connector *connector,
 			       vsdb_info.min_refresh_rate_hz,
 			       vsdb_info.max_refresh_rate_hz, freesync_capable);
 
+		/*
+		 * The amdgpu-side parse_hdmi_amd_vsdb() relies on the DMUB/DMCU
+		 * firmware to report the AMD VSDB; on some RDNA4 parts the
+		 * firmware does not detect it. Fall back to the DRM-core parse
+		 * (drm_edid.c), which reads the AMD VSDB directly and already
+		 * populated connector->display_info.amd_vsdb.
+		 */
+		if (!freesync_capable &&
+		    connector->display_info.amd_vsdb.freesync_supported) {
+			amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq =
+				connector->display_info.amd_vsdb.min_frame_rate;
+			amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq =
+				connector->display_info.amd_vsdb.max_frame_rate;
+			if (amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq -
+			    amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq > 10)
+				freesync_capable = true;
+
+			connector->display_info.monitor_range.min_vfreq =
+				amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq;
+			connector->display_info.monitor_range.max_vfreq =
+				amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq;
+
+			/* The later freesync_vcp_code/mccs check (see the
+			 * freesync_capable = false reset below) would undo this;
+			 * satisfy it with the DRM-core VCP info so the
+			 * fallback result sticks.
+			 */
+			if (connector->display_info.amd_vsdb.freesync_vcp_code) {
+				sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code =
+					connector->display_info.amd_vsdb.freesync_vcp_code;
+				sink->mccs_caps.freesync_supported = true;
+			}
+
+			drm_dbg_driver(adev_to_drm(adev),
+				       "VRR: drm-edid amd_vsdb fallback: fs_sup=1 min=%d max=%d\n",
+				       amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq,
+				       amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq);
+		}
+
+
 		/*
 		 * If AMD VSDB didn't provide a valid FreeSync range, fall back to
 		 * the HDMI 2.1 VRR capability parsed from the HF-VSDB.
